   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law, in relation to requiring vine trimming\nfor the maintenance of utility poles",
    "basePrintNo": "S2988",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2988-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §119-d, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2988\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to requiring vine\ntrimming for the maintenance of utility poles\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRequires vine trimming for the maintenance of utility poles\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the public service law by adding new section 119-d\nwhich requires the commission to require the trimming of vines on utili-\nty poles throughout the state by the utility company or cable television\ncompany that owns such utility poles.\n\nSection 2 states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill requires utility and cable television companies to maintain\ntheir utility poles for vine growth. When accompanied by severe weather,\nutility poles with excessive amounts of vegetation pose a safety concern\nfor both pedestrians and the property in its vicinity.\n\nCurrently, utility companies maintain their poles under a five year\nschedule. Adding the requirement that utility poles are maintained for\nvine growth lowers the likelihood that a consumer's service is inter-\nrupted and alleviates the safety concerns associated with excessive\nvines.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-2022: S7468/A10098 - Advanced to Third Reading/Died in Corpera-\ntions, Authorities and Commissions\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law. Effective immediately, the addition, amendment and/or\nrepeal of any rule or regulation necessary for the implementation of\nthis act or its effective date are authorized to be made and completed\non or 'before such effective, date.\n",
